# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# graphify knowledge graph (local artifact, contains absolute local paths)
graphify-out/

# crates/atomic/chrome-ui's real npm-installed dependencies (Preact/htm) -
# package.json/package-lock.json stay tracked, the installed packages
# themselves don't, same convention as any other npm project.
node_modules/

# shared_memory crate's Windows backing-file marker, dropped in the process's
# cwd when a shell.exe launched from apps/shell/ actually spawns a profile
# (see apps/shell/src/browser_view.rs's BrowserView::spawn_with_identity)
atomic-profile-*
atomic-shell-*

# impeccable design skill's own compiled binary (platform-specific, ~15MB)
# and generated font-index caches - regenerable local artifacts, not source,
# same reasoning graphify-out/ above already documents. The skill's real
# source (SKILL.md, reference/*.md, the JS scripts themselves) stays
# tracked.
.agents/skills/impeccable/scripts/bin/
.agents/skills/impeccable/scripts/data/font-index*.json
